#set enum(indent: 1em)

= Intoduction

The purpose of this document is to explain a tool for easily building pckages for the Odyssey Linux Distrobution.  The Odyssey LInux
distribution was build on top of the Void Linux Distrobution.

= Use Case

#table( 
	columns: 2,
	[*Name*], [*Value*],
	[Use Case Number], [1],
	[Preconditions], [ The container to build void packages is running 
		- All packages are installed that are needed to build pakcages 
		- Commmon directory between the host and the container],
	[Basic Flow], [
		+ In the container from the common directory execute a script that will build and place the package in the common directory
		+ On the host system, run script that will place the package in a repository] 
)

== Assumptions

+ The tool only creates packages for the x86_64 architecture

+ The packages will be built from a Github Repository

+ Only one package will be built at a time

+ The packages will be for the x64_64 type only.  Currently there are no 32 bit or MUSL packages in this repository.  The primary use of package repository is to contain packages for odyssey.


